      "message": "fix(post): Tormach lifts Z after each tool change before moving X/Y\n\nEvery Tormach mill tool change posted G53 G0 Z0, G30, T.. M6, G43 H..,\nthe spindle, then G0 X Y with no Z lift between. A bare G30 leaves Z at\nthe stored G30 height; one stored below the part top (the user's\nPathPilot Hub sim had machine Z -1.5611, the cause of #1594) rapids the\ntool sideways at that height into the part or the vise.\n\nstartPreamble now writes liftZ() (G53 G0 Z0, or the machine's stated\nsafe Z, #495) right after the G43 line, before the spindle start and the\nsection's first X/Y or A move. The tool-change G30 stays (PathPilot's\nconvention). The plasma and lathe G30s are kept with the reasons in\ndocs/decisions/1596-toolchange-lift.md; the lathe's diagonal approach\nfrom G30 is filed as #1604.\n\nPinned by tormach_toolchange_lift (every shipped Tormach mill, a stated\nsafe Z, the 4th-axis A index); tormach_safe_retract and\nprobe_spindle_stop updated. 33 NC goldens gain only G53 G0 Z0 lines (35).\n\nFixes #1596\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
